 "_about": "the gaulos -- the 'tub' the Greeks named the Phoenicians' round merchant ship: a beamy, deep hull with its stem and sternpost rising alike, a horse's head on the stem, a wicker fence round the open hold heaped with amphorae, one broad square sail brailed up to its yard and a crow's nest on the mast, two steering oars. (About 18-25 m; the Uluburun and Kyrenia wrecks are 15 m and smaller, the Ma'agan Michael 13 m -- the size estimated from the texts' cargoes of 100-400 t)",
